The session plan is written: two task files plus an issue-responses file in session_plan/. They aren't committed, because .gitignore excludes session_plan/, so git add refused. I assumed the harness reads them from disk and didn't force-add them. The plan's facts about yoagent 0.27.9 and the issue tracker came from grep and gh at planning time; nothing was built or run.

Task 1 — Part of #1202, the clause the owner bolded (product; bash_parse.rs, tools.rs, bash_parse_tests.rs, plus permissions.md)
• The fix: a command yoyo can't analyse will ask for confirmation instead of running. That covers a parse error, eval, or a command name produced by an expansion. It will ask even after the user answered "always", and even when an exact allow rule matches.
• Why: today {echo,hi} and l[s] don't parse in tree-sitter-bash, so no tree check ever sees them, and after one "always" answer they print ✓ Auto-approved.
• The task file quotes the owner's clause word for word and marks each part done or deferred. The title says "part of step 1", because step 2 is still open.
• `--yes` is deliberately left alone. It switches confirmation off entirely. The task posts that to the owner as an either/or: default A keeps --yes all-or-nothing; B refuses unanalyzable commands under it.
• Order inside the task: post the before-table on #1202 before the first edit, and the after-table plus the recall-control result right after the re-probe, before the full test run. It also counts how many ordinary valid commands would start asking.
• Test commands are harmless shapes only, because the Day 261 session was refused over a list of dangerous strings.

Task 2 — Fixes #1121 (the backlog-drain slot) (product; providers.rs, anthropic_preset_tests.rs)
• What's left on the ticket: one row. anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 is on the Bedrock model picker, but yoagent 0.27.9 can't resolve it to a Bedrock preset, so it runs on guessed limits.
• The fix: drop it from the list, and add a test that every listed Bedrock Claude id resolves a yoagent Bedrock preset, with a recall control.
• Also in the task: probe each listed id on the built binary and update the one existing assertion that pins opus-4-7 on the list. The user-facing reason goes in the renamed test's doc comment.

